<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore February non-oil exports fall 7.9 pct.</title>
<headline>Singapore February non-oil exports fall 7.9 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore's non-oil domestic exports fell a nominal 7.9 percent year-on-year in February  to Singapore $5.52 billion after falling 3.1 percent in January, the Trade Development Board (TDB) said on Thursday.</p>
<p>In real terms, non-oil exports fell 4.4 percent in February to S$7.12 billion after rising 1.4 percent in January.</p>
<p>A Reuters poll of 16 economist on Tuesday had forecast a 1.5 percent rise in the nominal figure.  </p>
<p>Trade in nominal terms, in bln S$ at current prices</p>
<p>(Year-on-year percentage changes given in parentheses)</p>
<p>				 February		 January</p>
<p>    Total trade	   24.28 (-8.6)	  30.86  (0.0)</p>
<p>    Exports		 11.60 (-6.1)	  15.07 (-1.6)</p>
<p>    Domestic exports     6.72 (-7.4)	   8.90 (-1.4)</p>
<p>    Oil			1.21 (-4.8)	   1.54  (7.6)</p>
<p>    Non-oil		  5.52 (-7.9)	   7.36 (-3.1)</p>
<p>    Re-exports	     4.88 (-4.3)	   6.17 (-1.8)</p>
<p>    Imports		 12.68(-10.7)	  15.79  (1.6)</p>
<p>Trade in real terms, in blns of S$ at 1990 prices</p>
<p>(Year-on-year percentage change given in parentheses)</p>
<p>				 February		 January</p>
<p>    Total trade	   28.86 (-6.3)	  36.47  (2.7)</p>
<p>    Exports		 14.25 (-4.2)	  18.53  (1.5)</p>
<p>    Domestic exports     8.68 (-6.5)	  11.52  (1.0)</p>
<p>    Oil			1.56(-15.0)	   1.97 (-0.7)</p>
<p>    Non-oil		  7.12 (-4.4)	   9.55  (1.4)</p>
<p>    Re-exports	     5.57 (-0.2)	   7.01  (2.4)</p>
<p>    Imports		 14.61 (-8.4)	  17.94  (3.9)</p>
